# The failover sweep's ratchet (ADR-0055 §11): every cell of the base
# catalogue that fails today, with the decision section that owns its
# correction. A change that makes a cell pass removes its line; a new failure
# is never added without its owner. The list only shrinks.
#
# The owner is read from the finding: a request or final a copy sends without
# the record of what the dead owner sent, a request into a dialog the other
# copy ended, and the non-2xx a copy owes a caller the dead primary answered
# §4; a deviation no declared window of §11 covers, §11; a PRACK, an owed ACK
# or an in-dialog request left unanswered §2; a 2xx repeat routed through the
# other owner §8; and any other finding of a split cell §7.

# The `applied` sync level writes a turn before its effects leave: a kill can
# leave the backup's record ahead of the wire.
media-leg/stalled-killed/t4-logged ADR-0055 §11 # a cap release leaves an answer the stalled backup never applies; the copy answers under a fresh To-tag
refer/primary-killed/t5-left ADR-0055 §3 # an outside service's answer taken by a turn the backup never applied; the copy waits with no answer deadline
refer/primary-killed/t8-left ADR-0055 §2 # the copy's seeded re-INVITE leaves before the ACK its record holds as sent
refer/primary-killed/t9-applied ADR-0055 §2 # the copy's seeded re-INVITE leaves before the ACK its record holds as sent
refer/primary-killed/t5-applied ADR-0055 §3 # an outside service's answer lost with the primary after the backup applied the request; the copy waits with no answer deadline
refer/primary-killed/t9-left ADR-0055 §11 # a party's 2xx repeat to the copy's re-sent INVITE carries other bytes than its first
refer/primary-killed/t10-left ADR-0055 §11 # a party's 2xx repeat to the copy's re-sent INVITE carries other bytes than its first
refer/primary-killed/t11-left ADR-0055 §11 # a party's 2xx repeat to the copy's re-sent INVITE carries other bytes than its first
reinvite/primary-killed/t5-left ADR-0055 §11 # a party's 2xx repeat to the copy's re-sent INVITE carries other bytes than its first
